---
// Recipe (entry) — Caldera recipes: Cast-iron skillet cornbread. Steps with timers, nutrition, Recipe JSON-LD.
---

<section id="recipe" class="section recipe">
  <!-- kit: recipe -->
  <article class="container">
    <header class="recipe-head">
      <div class="head-copy">
        <ul class="tags" role="list">
          <li>Bread</li>
          <li>Coals or oven</li>
          <li>Easy</li>
          <li>Vegetarian</li>
        </ul>
        <h1>Cast-iron skillet cornbread</h1>
        <p class="lead">Crisp-edged, barely sweet cornbread baked in a screaming-hot skillet over coals — or in the oven at home.</p>
        <p class="byline">By <a href="/authors/daniel-okafor">Daniel Okafor</a> · <span class="rating" aria-label="Rated 4.8 out of 5">★★★★★ 4.8</span></p>
        <dl class="facts">
          <div><dt>Prep</dt><dd>10 min</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Cook</dt><dd>25 min</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Rest</dt><dd>10 min</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Total</dt><dd>45 min</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Serves</dt><dd>8 <span class="yield">(one 10-inch skillet)</span></dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <img class="hero-img" src="https://picsum.photos/seed/skillet-cornbread/1600/1200" alt="A golden cornbread in a 10-inch cast iron skillet, one wedge cut out" width="3200" height="2400" />
    </header>

    <div class="recipe-body">
      <aside class="ingredients">
        <h2>Ingredients</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><span class="qty">240 g</span> medium-grind cornmeal</li>
          <li><span class="qty">125 g</span> plain flour</li>
          <li><span class="qty">2 tsp</span> baking powder</li>
          <li><span class="qty">1 tsp</span> fine salt</li>
          <li><span class="qty">2 tbsp</span> honey</li>
          <li><span class="qty">480 ml</span> buttermilk</li>
          <li><span class="qty">2</span> eggs, <span class="prep">beaten</span></li>
          <li><span class="qty">60 g</span> butter, <span class="prep">melted, plus 1 tbsp for the pan</span></li>
        </ul>
        <h3>To serve</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><span class="qty">2 tbsp</span> hot honey <span class="optional">(optional)</span></li>
          <li>flaky salt, <span class="prep">to taste</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Equipment</h3>
        <a class="equipment" href="/products/ridge-skillet">
          <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/caldera-ridge-skillet/240/240" alt="Ridge Skillet 10 inch" width="240" height="240" loading="lazy" />
          <span><strong>Ridge Skillet 10"</strong><br />$95</span>
        </a>
      </aside>

      <div class="method">
        <h2>Method</h2>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li class="step">
            <div class="step-text">
              <h3>Heat the pan</h3>
              <p>Set the skillet over medium coals or in a <strong>220°C</strong> oven with 1 tbsp butter inside for <strong>10 minutes</strong>.</p>
              <button type="button" class="timer" data-minutes="10" data-label="Preheat">⏱ Preheat · 10:00</button>
            </div>
            <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/cornbread-pan-heat/1200/900" alt="Butter foaming in a hot cast iron skillet" width="2400" height="1800" loading="lazy" />
          </li>
          <li class="step">
            <div class="step-text">
              <h3>Mix</h3>
              <p>Whisk the dry ingredients. Stir in the honey, buttermilk, eggs and melted butter until just combined — lumps are fine.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="step">
            <div class="step-text">
              <h3>Bake</h3>
              <p>Pour the batter into the sizzling pan. Cover with the lid and pile coals on top, or bake uncovered in the oven, for <strong>25 minutes</strong>.</p>
              <p class="tip"><strong>Tip:</strong> It's done when a skewer comes out clean and the edges pull away from the pan.</p>
              <button type="button" class="timer" data-minutes="25" data-label="Bake">⏱ Bake · 25:00</button>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="step">
            <div class="step-text">
              <h3>Rest</h3>
              <p>Rest 10 minutes in the pan so it slices cleanly. Drizzle with hot honey and flaky salt.</p>
              <button type="button" class="timer" data-minutes="10" data-label="Rest">⏱ Rest · 10:00</button>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="video">
          <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/3n1u3pTw1kM" title="Cast-iron skillet cornbread (YouTube video)" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
        </div>

        <div class="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>
          <p><strong>No buttermilk?</strong> Stir 1 tbsp lemon juice into 480 ml milk and wait 5 minutes.</p>
          <p>Keeps two days wrapped. Reheat wedges cut-side down in a dry skillet.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="nutrition">
          <h2>Nutrition <span>per serving</span></h2>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Calories</dt><dd>290</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Protein</dt><dd>7 g</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Fat</dt><dd>10 g</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Carbs</dt><dd>43 g</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Fibre</dt><dd>2 g</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Sodium</dt><dd>420 mg</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

